From d1b9d82bd74170d605c5a76bd7a4e21ea1603b81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 23:50:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] [feature](be) Refactor native stack collector to
 snapshot-remote-unwind
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the freeform per-slot atomic + poll-loop collector with a
two-phase coordinator that mirrors OceanBase's ob_signal_worker shape
under the snapshot-remote-unwind handler payload:

  1. acquire shared srunwind ctx try_lock (HTTP busy path)
  2. refresh /proc/self/maps via SrunwindProcMaps once
  3. iterate /proc/self/task via SYS_getdents64 (OB iter_task)
  4. per-thread under the lock:
     - refresh [stack] VMA from /proc/self/task/<tid>/maps
     - stamp anti-spoof req_id + target_tid
     - pipe2(O_CLOEXEC) for two-phase exchange
     - rt_tgsigqueueinfo(sival_ptr=req_id)
     - poll prepare-ack: worker has memcpy'd ucontext + 8 KiB stack
     - copy snapshot OUT of shared ctx into per-thread storage
     - write process-done on fd2_, poll exit-ack
     - close pipes, atomic_set_req_id(0)
  5. release the lock
  6. for each captured snapshot, run libunwind remote unwind via
     create_snapshot_addr_space + unw_init_remote + unw_step loop
  7. compute DSO offsets via SrunwindProcMaps + emit JSON response

The handler does NO libunwind work — the unwind cursor walks the
snapshot only on the coordinator side, per docs/phase2-plan.md:67-71.

Drops the freeform variant's per-slot atomics + tgkill fallback because
both are out of scope for an OB-mirroring coordinator: a single shared
ctx serializes per-thread iteration, and tgkill cannot carry the
anti-spoof req_id token. Stack snapshots survive past the next worker's
signal because each iteration copies the shared ctx buffer into
per-thread Snapshot storage before releasing the worker.

